{"name":"Hatching Chameleon","hex":"#cfebde","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hatching","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A method of shading areas of a drawing or diagram with fine parallel lines.","A group of birds, reptiles, fish, insects, etc., which emerge from their eggs at the same time."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of hatch"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hatching"},{"term":"chameleon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small to mid-size reptile, of the family Chamaeleonidae, and one of the best known lizard families able to change color and project its long tongue.","A person with inconstant behavior; one able to quickly adjust to new circumstances."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That changes or modifies its color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chameleon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hatching","blocks":[{"text":"Hatching is an artistic technique used to create tonal or shading effects by drawing, painting, or scribing closely spaced parallel lines. When lines are placed at an angle to one another, it is called cross-hatching. Hatching is also sometimes used to encode colours in monochromatic representations of colour images, particularly in heraldry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Veronica_detail.jpg/330px-Veronica_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hatching","wikidata":"Q2734755"},{"title":"Chameleon","blocks":[{"text":"Chameleons are a distinctive and highly specialized clade of Old World lizards with 200 species described as of June 2015. The members of this family are best known for their distinct range of colours, being capable of colour-shifting camouflage. The large number of species in the family exhibit considerable variability in their capacity to change colour. For some, it is more of a shift of brightness ; for others, a plethora of colour-combinations can be seen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Panther_Chameleon_738367_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Panther_Chameleon_738367_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","wikidata":"Q37686"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/AGAD_Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_%E2%80%93_The_Sudarium.jpg/500px-AGAD_Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_%E2%80%93_The_Sudarium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/AGAD_Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_%E2%80%93_The_Sudarium.jpg/1280px-AGAD_Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_%E2%80%93_The_Sudarium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/AGAD_Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_%E2%80%93_The_Sudarium.jpg/500px-AGAD_Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_%E2%80%93_The_Sudarium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAGAD_Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_%E2%80%93_The_Sudarium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cam_follower-stud_style.png/960px-Cam_follower-stud_style.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cam_follower-stud_style.png/1280px-Cam_follower-stud_style.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cam_follower-stud_style.png/960px-Cam_follower-stud_style.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACam_follower-stud_style.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Philadelphia_County_Prison_%28Moy