 lattice parameter indicated with black arrows.\n(c) Haematoxylin and eosin staining of a cross-section of white skin showing the epidermis and the two thick layers of iridophores.\n(d) TEM images of guanine nanocrystals in S-iridophores in the excited state and three-dimensional model of an FCC lattice (shown in two orientations).\n(e) TEM image of guanine nanocrystals in D-iridophores.[18]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColour_change_and_iridophore_types_in_panther_chameleons.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Erp%C3%A9tologie_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale%2C_ou%2C_Histoire_naturelle_compl%C3%A8te_des_reptiles_%28Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_skeleton%29.jpg/500px-Erp%C3%A9tologie_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale%2C_ou%2C_Histoire_naturelle_compl%C3%A8te_des_reptiles_%28Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_skeleton%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Erp%C3%A9tologie_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale%2C_ou%2C_Histoire_naturelle_compl%C3%A8te_des_reptiles_%28Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_skeleton%29.jpg/1280px-Erp%C3%A9tologie_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale%2C_ou%2C_Histoire_naturelle_compl%C3%A8te_des_reptiles_%28Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_skeleton%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Erp%C3%A9tologie_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale%2C_ou%2C_Histoire_naturelle_compl%C3%A8te_des_reptiles_%28Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_skeleton%29.jpg/500px-Erp%C3%A9tologie_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale%2C_ou%2C_Histoire_naturelle_compl%C3%A8te_des_reptiles_%28Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_skeleton%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Skeleton of common chameleon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErp%C3%A9tologie_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale%2C_ou%2C_Histoire_naturelle_compl%C3%A8te_des_reptiles_(Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_skeleton).jpg"}],"sounds":{"hatching":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimed